@@ -32,3 +32,13 @@ member by member (a non-object target is treated as `{}`); a `null` member remov
 patch value, including an array, replaces the target. Neither argument is modified and the result shares
 no structure with them. `__proto__` and similar keys are treated as plain members. Note that a merge patch
 cannot set a member to `null`. Any JSON value is a valid patch, so it never throws.
+
+## Creating a JSON Patch (RFC 6902)
+
+`createPatch(from, to)` (exported from `src/index.ts`) returns a JSON Patch (`add`, `remove` and `replace`
+operations, RFC 6902 section 4) such that `applyPatch(from, patch)` equals `to`; it is empty when the two
+are equal (RFC 6902 section 4.6 equality, so object member order is irrelevant). The patch describes only
+what differs: objects are compared member by member and arrays item by item. An item added to or removed
+from an array is a single `add` or `remove` and the items around it are left alone; an item that moves is
+a `remove` followed by an `add`. Neither argument is modified and the patch shares no structure with them.
+It never throws.
